    costs=[('Frozen source/input preparation',plan['preparation_seconds']),('Pre-E independent assertion/native-boundary gate',load(OUT/'input-audit.json')['seconds']),('Fresh checker fixture reruns',summary['fixtures']['seconds']),('Repeated pre-run assertion/native-boundary gate within producer',summary['pre_run_gate_seconds']),('Four E binary search processes',sum(o['e_measurement']['wall_seconds'] for o in summary['observations'])),('Four complete-check workers including startup/serialization',sum(o['proof_check']['process_wall_seconds'] for o in summary['observations'])),('Four serialized full-replay workers',sum(o['proof_replay']['process_wall_seconds'] for o in summary['observations'])),('Whole capped producer (contains the preceding components)',summary['seconds']),('Independent post-result full replay/source/input audit',audit['seconds']),('Actual-certificate corruption audit',mut['seconds']),('Additional fresh-directory reproduction producer',qa['producer_seconds']),('Additional reproduction full replay audit',qa['audit_seconds']),('Additional reproduction corruption audit',qa['mutation_seconds'])]
    costrows=''.join('<tr><td>'+esc(n)+'</td><td>'+seconds(v)+'</td></tr>' for n,v in costs);census=mut['proof_census']
    page=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Derived-premise incidence · external E control</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="report.css"><script>window.MathJax={tex:{inlineMath:[['\\(','\\)']],displayMath:[['\\[','\\]']]},options:{skipHtmlTags:['script','noscript','style','textarea','pre','code']}};</script><script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-chtml.js"></script><style>main{max-width:1140px;margin:auto;padding:24px}section{margin:40px 0}.formula{overflow:auto;max-width:100%;margin:16px 0}.proof-line{display:grid;grid-template-columns:32px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd;padding:18px 0}.proof-line>span{border-top:4px solid #258571}.input>span{border-color:#347bba}.negation>span{border-color:#c08b38}.annotation{color:#526968;font-size:13px}.pin{overflow-wrap:anywhere}pre{white-space:pre;overflow:auto;max-height:400px;font-size:11px}details{margin:14px 0}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd}select{max-width:100%}[hidden]{display:none!important}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}.flow>div{padding:20px;background:#eef4ee;border-top:4px solid #258571}.flow strong{display:block;margin-bottom:9px}@media(max-width:650px){.flow{grid-template-columns:1fr}.proof-line{grid-template-columns:22px minmax(0,1fr)}}</style></head><body><main><nav><a href="index.html#goals">Research program</a> · <a href="hilbert_boundary_transfer.html#reader">Separate native transfer notebook</a></nav><h1>E proves the two derived-premise incidence assertions.</h1><p>Four fresh searches pass complete independent checking and replay. The delayed-common assertion has \(38\) returned lines; the coupled reversed-line assertion has \(41\). Each is repeated twice in the predeclared interleaved order, with no lemma input or supplied target derivation. These are external first-order proofs; they are not native Wang certificates or GCTS/RL discoveries.</p><div class="flow"><div><strong>Exact symbolic hypotheses</strong>Each input contains the signature, universally quantified guarded I.2, its three closed hypotheses and the identical target.</div><div><strong>Automatic E search</strong>No coordinates, receptor inventory, marked tiling, induction schema or target proof sequence is supplied.</div><div><strong>Every returned line checked</strong>Exact inputs, target negation, all logical transformations and contradiction receive independently replayed certificates.</div></div><section id="comparison"><h2>Same assertions, different proof languages</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Assertion</th><th>Run</th><th>Lines</th><th>E seconds</th><th>Check seconds</th><th>Replay seconds</th><th>E peak RSS bytes</th><th>Check peak RSS bytes</th></tr>__ROWS__</table></div><p>E already finds both assertions from their axioms alone. Its search latency is much smaller on this shared-host measurement, while complete checking costs several seconds per proof. This supplies an established-method control; it does not establish a controlled speed ratio, mathematical novelty or a GCTS advantage over E.</p><p>The native short and sufficient row regions express exactly the same assertion. E has no fixed proof-row boundary and may instantiate the quantified uniqueness axiom beyond the native finite catalog. Native promotion changes the inventory; learned ordering changes proposal priority within an identical inventory. Their costs and certificate languages differ.</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Native sufficient-boundary recipient</th><th>Policy</th><th>Attempts</th><th>Search outcome</th><th>Native certification</th><th>Search seconds</th><th>Model setup seconds</th></tr>__NATIVE_ROWS__</table></div><p>The separately completed native experiment retains a useful deterministic signal: learned ordering reaches the promoted receptor at \(24\) and \(40\) attempts where the equal-inventory fixed ordering reaches its \(600\)-attempt cutoff. This is evidence about these two recipients, with all fallback candidates retained. It is not a general proof-search superiority claim; a cutoff is an unknown, not a disproof. The native study’s six finite exhaustions and thirteen search unknowns remain unchanged.</p></section><section id="statement"><h2>Exact theory and human-readable assertions</h2>__STATEMENTS__<p>Objects and predicates are uninterpreted. The symbols are not coordinates: the logic can concern any objects satisfying these axioms. Ordinary constants need not denote different objects; distinctness of the two common points is an explicit hypothesis inside the guarded uniqueness condition. Existence, order, congruence, parallelism and continuity axioms are absent.</p><p>The English below translates actual formulas and clause rows. In both input families, the common-point condition must first be obtained from the readiness hypothesis. In the coupled case, the additional incidence also depends on that condition. Those dependencies are hypotheses, not an input derivation.</p></section><section id="reader"><h2>Read each actual proof line</h2><p>Blue rows are exact inputs, amber is target negation, and green rows are independently checked consequences. Clause variables are explicitly universally closed. These colors identify external proof roles; they do not depict Wang tiles or GCTS markings. All formulas are decoded from the actual TSTP output. There are no fresh witness introductions in these four returned proofs.</p><label for="proof-choice">Actual derivation</label> <select id="proof-choice">__OPTIONS__</select>__PANELS__</section><section id="checking"><h2>Complete checking and conservative limitations</h2><p>The previously published focused/shared-context adapter is unchanged. It validates every original role and formula, strictly earlier parents, target negation, predicate/function signatures, shared context and every logical consequence. Exact universal instances can establish a refutation; satisfiability of a finite sample never establishes an unrestricted quantified entailment. Unsupported inferences or budget exhaustion remain unknown.</p><p>Independent replay covers __LINES__ returned lines, __FOCUSED__ focused first-order trees and __PROPOSITIONAL__ propositional trees. Every actual tree has an altered-conflict test; focused certificates also undergo relation-digest and substitution tests. All __CORRUPTIONS__ corruptions are rejected, including altered supplied axioms, missing final parents, wrong input identity and unexported theory features. Existing quantifier-order, finite-domain, dependency, freshness and capture fixtures were rerun before E.</p><p>The parser, clausifier and replay implementation are trusted code, not a formally verified kernel. The <a href="https://tptp.org/UserDocs/TPTPLanguage/TPTPLanguage.shtml">official TPTP language</a>, E’s <a href="https://github.com/eprover/eprover/blob/3b7afc70fe77d3118bb95144c4735ca45f5f31cf/CLAUSES/ccl_tcnf.c">pinned clausifier</a> and <a href="https://github.com/eprover/eprover/blob/3b7afc70fe77d3118bb95144c4735ca45f5f31cf/README.md">README</a> document the separate certificate language. E’s bundled <code>checkproof</code> skips nonclausal steps; its status is not our acceptance basis.</p></section><section id="costs"><h2>Preparation, search and replay costs</h2><table><tr><th>Component</th><th>Seconds</th></tr>__COSTS__</table><p>The measured producer has a \(180\)-second cap including fixtures, the pre-run binding gate and all four E/check/replay trials. Each E process requests \(10\) CPU seconds, \(12\) wall seconds and \(1024\) MiB. Each certificate worker has \(20\) wall seconds, with the unchanged sampled \(1\)-GiB self-RSS cutoff and bounded instance search. There are no new unknown or unexecuted runs. The additional fresh-directory reproduction is QA, not another measured repetition.</p><p>Nested timers are not additive. Check/replay process clocks include startup and serialization. Read-only frozen-byte validation before the producer timer, manual infrastructure work, source acquisition and initial E configuration remain unmeasured; the separate input gate and preparation clocks are retained. Warm caches and concurrent work affect latency attribution.</p><p>The geometry provenance is reused, not rerun: __NATIVE_QUERIES__ native computations, __NATIVE_STEPS__ microsteps, __NATIVE_PRODUCTION__ seconds production and __NATIVE_REPLAY__ seconds independent replay. Its __NATIVE_SEARCH__ seconds search and __NATIVE_SETUP__ seconds model setup, all original unknowns and prior inventory/policy costs remain in the native report. __INHERITED__</p><p>The pinned E build is reused. Its recorded rebuild cost was approximately \(30.21\) seconds and \(146.45\) MiB RSS; source acquisition/configuration was unmeasured. The binary reports a <code>DEBUG</code> version and a different embedded revision from the pinned checkout; the exact version and identities remain in the plan. Binary SHA-256: <code class="pin">__BINARY__</code>.</p></section><section id="evidence"><h2>Exact reproducible evidence</h2><p><a href="external_hilbert_transfer_control_plan.json">Frozen plan</a> · <a href="external_hilbert_transfer_control_summary.json">Compact results and costs</a> · <a href="external_hilbert_transfer_control_audit.json">Complete independent audit</a> · <a href="external_hilbert_transfer_control_mutations.json">Actual-certificate corruptions</a> · <a href="external_hilbert_transfer_control_data.json.gz">Every source, input, process, line certificate and native provenance binding</a>.</p><p>Each proof also has an individual complete certificate and original TSTP download. Opening a certificate card loads its exact saved JSON; display loading does not check or change proof validity. All measured scientific sources and earlier published exports remain unchanged. Root owns integration and publication.</p><details><summary>Reproduce in a fresh private directory with the pinned binary</summary><pre>PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/private/tmp/gcts-native-wang-pycache python3 research/gcts-rl-renewal/external_hilbert_transfer_reproduce.py --output .gcts-active/external-hilbert-transfer-reproduce --e /private/tmp/gcts-external-eprover-20261011/PROVER/eprover</pre></details></section></main><script>const certificates=new Map();async function getCertificate(file){if(!certificates.has(file))certificates.set(file,(async()=>{const r=await fetch(file);if(!r.ok)throw new Error('Certificate download failed: '+r.status);const b=await r.arrayBuffer();const stream=new Blob([b]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip'));return JSON.parse(await new Response(stream).text());})());return certificates.get(file);}for(const d of document.querySelectorAll('details.certificate'))d.addEventListener('toggle',async()=>{if(!d.open||d.dataset.loaded)return;const p=d.querySelector('.certificate-output');p.textContent='Loading exact saved certificate…';try{const all=await getCertificate(d.dataset.file);p.textContent=JSON.stringify({source:all.records[Number(d.dataset.index)].source,certificate:all.certificate.checks[Number(d.dataset.index)]},null,2);d.dataset.loaded='true';}catch(e){p.textContent=String(e)+'\nUse the complete certificate download above.';}});document.getElementById('proof-choice').addEventListener('change',async function(){for(const p of document.querySelectorAll('.proof-panel'))p.hidden=p.id!=='proof-'+this.value;if(window.MathJax?.typesetPromise)await MathJax.typesetPromise([document.getElementById('proof-'+this.value)]);});</script></body></html>'''
    inherited='<details><summary>Inherited native inventory, source promotion and transferred policy costs</summary><pre>'+esc(json.dumps(native['prior_cost_provenance'],indent=2))+'</pre><p>Aggregate and component clocks overlap and must not be summed as disjoint cold costs.</p></details>'
    values=dict(ROWS=''.join(rows),NATIVE_ROWS=''.join(native_rows),STATEMENTS=''.join(statements),OPTIONS=''.join(options),PANELS=''.join(panels),COSTS=costrows,LINES=num(census['lines']),FOCUSED=num(census['focused_trees']),PROPOSITIONAL=num(census['propositional_trees']),CORRUPTIONS=num(len(mut['corruptions'])),NATIVE_QUERIES=num(native_audit['fresh_native_queries']),NATIVE_STEPS=num(native_audit['fresh_native_micro_steps']),NATIVE_PRODUCTION=seconds(native_audit['fresh_native_production_seconds']),NATIVE_REPLAY=seconds(native_audit['fresh_native_replay_seconds']),NATIVE_SEARCH=seconds(sum(o['search_seconds'] for o in native['observations'])),NATIVE_SETUP=seconds(sum(o['setup_seconds'] for o in native['observations'])),INHERITED=inherited,BINARY=plan['prover_binary_sha256'])
